{
  "id": 143147850,
  "iid": 6349,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Draft: TLS: Fix TLS tunneled over TLS, make layer numbers stable",
  "description": "Address the underlying issue that was worked around in #16109.\nWhen desegmenting TLS, some segments entirely lie within multisegment\nPDUs that end in some later segment. This can only be determined by\ncalling the subdissector, so the subdissector is called on the first\npass but not future passes, once the MSP is already created.\n\nIn those cases, the subdissector reports success but sets\npinfo->desegment_len to a nonzero value while leaving\npinfo->desegment_offset as zero. When this happens, remove any protocol\nlayers added by the subdissector on the first pass, so that the layer\nnumbers from that point in the stack will be the same as on subsequent\npasses.\n\nRemove the workaround for #16109. Fix #17977.",
  "state": "closed",
