        {
          "id": 926962913,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There's a general problem with the layer numbers not always being the same in the first pass and subsequent passes, since most dissectors (understandably) assume that they will be.\n\nTCP desegmentation is the most notable case, though I've seen it in MPEG2TS dissection when exceptions are hit because of packet loss. (Since TS streams don't have any kind of fragment ID and just add fragments in order, missing packets really mess things up.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-04-28T01:00:55.043Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-04-28T01:00:55.043Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 143147850,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
